<task id="024" project="email-communication-intelligence-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>SPE content dedup Tier-1 — quickXorHash detector on SpeFileStore, all upload paths</title>
    <phase>2 Pillar C — De-duplication</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>BFF code introducing a new detector service on the SPE facade + hooking every upload path; correctness-sensitive (silent duplicate suppression); tags include bff-api. code-review + adr-check MANDATORY at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>New content-dedup detector spanning all upload paths through the ADR-007 facade with a notify-never-silent contract and a spike-gated hash identity — high blast radius across the storage seam; per project CLAUDE.md C3 is an Opus task.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies `Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs` + `Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs` (shared storage/upload surface — contended with compose / messaging / notification-spine). Sequential, main-session; `/conflict-check` before PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>023</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, spe, dedup, storage</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
