  <prompt>Implement FR-C3 Tier-1 (exact hash-equality): a content-dedup detector routed THROUGH the `SpeFileStore` facade (ADR-007 — no direct Graph in callers) that reads `quickXorHash` from `driveItem.file.hashes`, checks the task-023 `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash` index, and on a byte-identical hit does NOT create a second canonical document — instead it notifies (never silent) and links/opens-canonical. Hook the detector at ALL upload paths INCLUDING the email-attachment path (`OfficeDocumentPersistence`). Absorb the `sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1` design. Tier-2 (near-dup) is explicitly OUT of scope here (spike-2-gated fast-follow).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF developer with SharePoint Embedded expertise. Reach SPE ONLY via `SpeFileStore` (ADR-007). Follow ADR-045, ADR-010/032 (DI), ADR-027 strictly. Use the `spe-integration` skill for facade patterns.</role>
  <goal>Uploading byte-identical content twice via ANY path (Assistant persist, Compose save, email-attachment) is detected at/before persist and does not create a second canonical document (Tier-1); on a hit the user is notified (never silent) and the upload is hash-linked / canonical-opened; the hash read + dedup route through `SpeFileStore` (no direct Graph in callers); all non-fatal (a hashing/detect failure never fails the upload). Unit + seam tests prove no second document on byte-identical content.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-C3 absorbs `projects/sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1/` (design-only, no code). Task 023 created the indexed `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash`. This task builds the detector: on upload, obtain the SPE `quickXorHash` (via the facade — `driveItem.file.hashes`; `sha256Hash` is DEPRECATED), look up an equal hash on `sprk_document`, and on a hit suppress the second canonical document while NOTIFYING (never silent) and linking. It hooks every upload entry — critically the email-attachment path (`OfficeDocumentPersistence`), which is the R2-specific extension over the sdap-r1 scope. The `sprk_document` model mapping for the new column lives in `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs`. Uses **gate-after-write** (owner 2026-08-05): read the `quickXorHash` from the driveItem AFTER upload completes, then reconcile against the `sprk_canonicalhash` index + notify — no pre-write spike gate. Depends only on task 023 (the column). Tier-2 near-dup (`documentVector3072` "Find Similar") is deferred OUT of R2 (exact-hash Tier-1 only) — do NOT build it here.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs (add the hash-read / dedup-lookup facade method)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs (email-attachment upload path hook)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs (sprk_canonicalhash mapping on the document model)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/... content-dedup detector service (new)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1/README.md + analysis.md (absorbed design)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/agent-memory/researcher/spe-dedup-content-identity-2026-07.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <!-- Task 001 (SPE spike 1) removed: gate-after-write (owner decision 2026-08-05) — read quickXorHash from the driveItem AFTER upload completes; no pre-write spike gate. -->
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">The indexed `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash` column the detector reads/writes.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SCOPE: SPE access. The hash read + any Graph interaction MUST route through `SpeFileStore`; callers (detector, OfficeDocumentPersistence) MUST NOT touch Graph directly. Add a facade method for the hash/dedup read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: gate-after-write (owner decision 2026-08-05). The detector reads `quickXorHash` from the driveItem metadata AFTER the upload completes (never a pre-write gate), then reconciles against the `sprk_canonicalhash` index and notifies (never silent). A brief transient duplicate blob is ACCEPTABLE — reconciliation + notify happen post-upload. There is no spike gate; do not block on spike 1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: hit behavior. On a byte-identical hit, NOTIFY (never silent) and open-canonical / proceed-hash-linked; do NOT silently drop the upload. Content divergence graduates a copy to its own document (Tier-1 = exact-equality only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: coverage. Hook the detector at ALL upload paths — Assistant persist, Compose save, AND the email-attachment path (`OfficeDocumentPersistence`). Missing the email-attachment path is a spec miss (R2-specific).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: identity. Use `quickXorHash` from `driveItem.file.hashes`; `sha256Hash` is DEPRECATED on SPE and MUST NOT be the identity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">SCOPE: detector. Hashing/detection MUST be non-fatal — a failure logs + degrades (upload proceeds without dedup), never throws out of the upload path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE: the new detector service. Register unconditionally; if config-gated, use the Null-Object/kill-switch pattern (ADR-032). No asymmetric `if(flag){AddScoped}` registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Tier-2. Near-dup / `documentVector3072` "Find Similar" is OUT of scope — spike-2-gated fast-follow. Do NOT implement it here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10-BFF">SCOPE: this BFF change. PR carries Placement Justification (new detector extends the SPE seam in place — no new microservice); report publish-size absolute + delta (≤60 MB ceiling); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE: tests. Add a dedup seam test under `tests/integration/seam/Communication/**` (or the storage seam path) proving byte-identical upload via each path creates no second document; update unit tests. KEEP path; no banned test shapes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: coordination. `/conflict-check` against compose / messaging / notification-spine before the PR (shared SpeFileStore / Office surface).</constraint>
  </constraints>

