      <pattern name="Absorbed dedup design" location="projects/sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1/">The detector design (two-tier, notify-never-silent, copy-graduates-on-divergence) to absorb; R2 adds the email-attachment path.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load POML + project CLAUDE.md + spec FR-C3/NFR-04/NFR-08 + ADR-007/045/010/032 + sdap-r1 design + researcher SPE memo. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL. Confirm task 023 column active. Apply gate-after-write (owner 2026-08-05): read quickXorHash from the driveItem AFTER upload completes, then reconcile against the index + notify (never silent); a brief transient duplicate blob is accepted. No spike-1 gate. Invoke task-execute + spe-integration.</step>
    <step order="1">Add a `SpeFileStore` facade method to read `quickXorHash` for a persisted/uploaded driveItem (via `driveItem.file.hashes`) — callers stay Graph-free.</step>
    <step order="2">Map `sprk_canonicalhash` on the `sprk_document` model in `Models.cs`; write the hash on document create.</step>
    <step order="3">Build the content-dedup detector service: given a new upload's quickXorHash, look up an equal `sprk_document.sprk_canonicalhash`; on a hit, suppress the second canonical document, notify (never silent), and link/open-canonical. Register unconditionally (ADR-010/032). Wrap non-fatal (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="4">Hook the detector at ALL upload paths: Assistant persist, Compose save, and the email-attachment path (`OfficeDocumentPersistence`). Verify each entry calls it exactly once.</step>
    <step order="5">Add seam tests: byte-identical upload via each path → no second document; hit → notification emitted; a hashing failure → upload proceeds (non-fatal). Update unit tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Build/test/publish; record publish-size delta + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="7">Step 9.5: code-review + adr-check; PR carries Placement Justification + size/CVE + a note that Tier-2 is deferred (spike 2).</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation (esp. spike-1 gate-timing decision) in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a duplicate is detected, the detector MUST notify + link/graduate the upload (reconcile post-write) — it MUST NEVER silently suppress or drop a document. If the reconcile+notify path cannot be made reliable such that a duplicate could be silently swallowed, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6/§6.5 (silent data-loss risk).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No content-dedup service anywhere in the upload pipeline (grep of `Services/**` + `Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs` shows storage/persist but no hash-based dedup). `sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1` is design-only (code-free).</existing>
    <extension>No — absorb the sdap-r1 design as a new detector. It is a distinct cross-cutting responsibility (content identity across containers/paths) that no existing persist method owns; bolting it into each persist caller would fork the logic across paths. One detector on the facade + one hook per path is the minimal, non-duplicated surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the detector, byte-identical files (incl. duplicate email attachments across N captures) create N canonical documents in SPE with no dedup authority — the exact FR-C3 failure. Storage + review surfaces fill with silent duplicates.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish; publish-size; CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="spe-integration">Facade patterns for SPE hash access</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeFileStore.cs (facade hash method) + new detector service</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs (email-attachment hook) + Models.cs mapping</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/** + tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/**</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given byte-identical content uploaded twice via the Assistant-persist path, when the second persists, then it is detected at/before persist and NO second canonical document is created (Tier-1).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a duplicate email attachment via the email-attachment path (`OfficeDocumentPersistence`), when persisted, then it is deduped (no second document) — the R2-specific path is covered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a byte-identical hit, when detected, then the user is NOTIFIED (never silent) and the upload is hash-linked / canonical-opened.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the detector runs, when it reads the SPE hash, then it does so via `SpeFileStore` (no direct Graph in the detector or OfficeDocumentPersistence) — ADR-007.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (non-fatal): Given hashing/detection throws, when an upload runs, then the exception is caught + logged and the upload proceeds without a second document being blocked erroneously.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tier-2 (near-dup / documentVector3072) is NOT implemented in this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit + seam tests pass; build green; publish size ≤60 MB with delta reported; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-C3 Tier-1 + NFR-04. Opus per project CLAUDE.md. Absorbs sdap-file-duplication-detector-r1. Gate-after-write (owner 2026-08-05): read quickXorHash from the driveItem post-upload, reconcile + notify, accept a brief transient duplicate blob; no spike-1 gate. Depends only on 023 (column). Tier-2 (near-dup / documentVector3072) is deferred OUT of R2 (exact-hash Tier-1 only; owner 2026-08-05) — do NOT build it here. Email-attachment path coverage is the R2-specific extension — do not omit it.</notes>

